  kuayle wiki list
    List pages (registry days are hidden unless --registry)
  kuayle wiki tree
    Show the page tree (folders and nesting)
  kuayle wiki read
    Read a page
  kuayle wiki create
    Create a page or folder
  kuayle wiki update
    Update a page's title and/or content
  kuayle wiki delete
    Delete a page
  kuayle wiki move
    Move a page under a parent (or top level) at a position
  kuayle wiki history
    List a page's revisions, newest first
  kuayle wiki restore
    Restore a page to a revision from its history
  kuayle registry append
    Add an entry to today's (UTC) registry page
  kuayle registry feed
    Show registry days, newest first
  kuayle registry overview
    List AI overviews of the registry, newest first
  kuayle registry generate-overview
    Generate an AI overview for a period (at most 31 days)
  kuayle usage
    Show command reference
  kuayle completion
    Generate shell completion script
  kuayle self-update
    Check for updates or update the binary
## Name Resolution

  Names accept: UUID (passthrough), human-readable name, or identifier.
  Names resolved via batch fetch + case-insensitive match.
  In-process memo + disk cache (5min TTL, --no-cache to disable).
  Multiple names resolved in parallel (tokio::join!).
  On failure: lists available candidates, exit code 3.

## Wiki and Registry

  wiki/registry commands need --team <name|key|id> or --project <name|id>.
  Content is HTML or Markdown (--content, or --file PATH|-).
  Token scopes: wiki:read to read, wiki:write to change.

## Exit Codes

  0  Success
  1  Generic error
  2  Authentication failure
  3  Resource not found
  4  Validation error
  5  Permission denied
  6  Rate limited
  7  Network / server unreachable

## Output Format

  --format human   Human-readable tables and text (default when TTY).
  --format json    Machine-readable JSON.
  Default: auto-detect — JSON when piped, human when interactive.
  JSON mode: errors are also JSON.
